\date{2024-08-12}
\taxon{definition}
\title{\universe{P}-semiextensional semicategory}
\author{Fredrik Bakke}
\import{common}

\p{
Given a [[hott-000K]] \universe{P}, a \universe{P}-\concept{semiextensional semicategory} is a [[fb-0034]] \category{C} such that the total types
##{\sigma-type{x:\category{C}}{(a \cong_\category{C} x)} \quad\text{and}\quad \sigma-type{x:\category{C}}{(x \cong_\category{C} a)}}
are in #{\universe{P}} for all objects #{a} in \category{C}.
}
